regfile eHI3536D_HDMI_ctrl {
    name = "HDMI TX ctrl, Hi3536D V100 / HDMI v2 (hisiv100)";
    desc = "TX control (reset/power, SCDC FSM, interrupts). Offsets are relative to the sub-block base 0x13000000 (HDMI TX window 0x13000000 + 0x0). Provenance: PROVEN (vendor code): register names, offsets, field names/bit ranges and reset (INIT) values come from the machine-generated register headers of the vendor HDMI v2 driver (nManager-generated hdmi_reg_ctrl.h, product/hiosd/hdmi/hdmi_v2/drv/hal in the vendor U-Boot tree for the Hi3536D/Hi3536C/Hi3531D/Hi3521D family, source: sources/openipc-u-boot-hi3536dv100); the Hi3536D V100 maps the window at 0x13000000 per its hdmi_product_define.h and the closed hi3536dv100_hdmi.ko symbol names (HDMI_TX_S_*_REGS_TYPE_Init) agree. INFERRED: access types. Of the 503 register definitions in the vendor headers only 38 carry an ATTR (all RW); the others have none, so fields are modelled read/write except reserved/rsv fields and registers whose names mark them read-only by convention where the vendor hal/drv C sources call the accessors (203 registers) a register only ever read is modelled sw=r and the call-site counts are in each register description; for the other registers the name convention (SW_VER*, HW_INFO/HW_VERSION/HW_FEATURE, _STATUS, _STAT, _STATE, _OUT<n>: sw=r) is used. The 8051 MCU window (mcu sub-block) is modelled the same way and its function is inferred from the HDCP2X_* names only and hardware behavior; nothing run on hardware. NOT in the data sheet (no HDMI TX chapter)." ;
    reg {
        name = "TX_PWD_RST_CTRL";
        desc = "TX_PWD_RST_CTRL (offset 0x10 in this sub-block, absolute 0x13000010). Reset INIT 0x00000400. PROVEN: vendor register header. Driver usage (vendor hal/drv C, uncommented call sites): 0 Get, 8 Set (hdmi_hal_ctrl.c, hdmi_hal_hdcp22.c): only written by the driver (kept RW: a write-only register cannot be told from an unread one). ";
